{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1497028-deviant-stretchy-variations","id":1497028,"title":"Deviant: Stretchy variations?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-13T15:49:42-08:00","id":1497028,"title":"Deviant: Stretchy variations?","content":"So, the time has come in my DC universe to build the Doom Patrol. Browsing the variations, I couldn't find an analogue to the limb stretching abilities of Elastigirl and Mr. Fantastic variety. Its possible it is tucked away somewhere in a variation that I hadnt noticed, but I think theres a possibility that there simply isn't one.<br /> <br /> Can anyone help me out? Did I overlook it? Or am I going to have to sort if build my own? I have one idea in mind already, in case nothing else comes up. Basically, the power is.. more or less a weaker version of Telekinesis. It would have pretty much the same abilities as Telekinesis. The only differences would be that a) the deviant can't use the power through glass or other solid objects, b) the effect of stretching flesh is considerably more obvious and disturbing than invisible forces, and c) stetched limbs could theoretically be cut off, releasing the object/person from control. <br /> <br /> Does anyone have any advice or experience with this? I really thought that Crazy Jane wouldve been the hard Doomer to recreate, not Rita.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-13T17:48:57-08:00","id":1497043,"title":"","content":"I don't have the Deviant book with me right now, but couldn't those limitations be.. whats the word, Scars? Those limitations you can take, like needing a specific fuel or the power stops working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-13T18:32:44-08:00","id":1497051,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27258_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27258\" data-vbnamecard=\"27258\">Cauthon</a> has the right idea. Just refluff Telekinesis with appropriate Scars entangled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-13T19:33:38-08:00","id":1497060,"title":"","content":"The closest thing to that is the Deviation &quot;Target Restriction&quot;, but even that is slightly off. Nothing quite works mechanically. Concentration is mechanically pretty close to what Im going for. Ive got her Mimicry entangled with Concentration, too (to reflect that Rita has to mentally keep herself together or she turns into goo). I guess I could add the Target Restriction Deviation for +1, the restriction being no targets under any form of cover..? <br /> <br /> As a side note, she already has Identifier at Universal level--using any of her Variations leaves bits of her goo, fingerprints, dna, etc on stuff. Shes also already got Conspicuous Appearance maxed out as well (due to her.. giant hideous blobbiness).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-13T20:57:28-08:00","id":1497065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1497028-deviant-stretchy-variations#post1497028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only differences would be that a) the deviant can't use the power through glass or other solid objects</div> </div> </div> </div>Directed Variations cannot ordinarily penetrate cover, transparent or otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> b) the effect of stretching flesh is considerably more obvious and disturbing than invisible forces, </div> </div> </div>Easily half the point of Overt/Subtle being a binary category innate to the Variation or Scar is to avoid splitting hairs over how obvious a Variation or Scar is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> c) stetched limbs could theoretically be cut off, releasing the object/person from control. </div> </div> </div>Removing a mechanical arm with a Disarm action is an example provided in the Common Deviation of Power Failure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-13T23:55:44-08:00","id":1497074,"title":"","content":"Would a combination of <i>Boneless</i> and <i>Brachiation</i> work for you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-14T02:46:11-08:00","id":1497080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1497028-deviant-stretchy-variations?p=1497065#post1497065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Directed Variations cannot ordinarily penetrate cover, transparent or otherwise.<br /> <br /> Easily half the point of Overt/Subtle being a binary category innate to the Variation or Scar is to avoid splitting hairs over how obvious a Variation or Scar is.<br /> <br /> Removing a mechanical arm with a Disarm action is an example provided in the Common Deviation of Power Failure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh dang, I had forgotten that Directed Variations can't penetrate cover. Woof, that makes some psychic type powers far less useful (telepathy to a degree, telekinesis especially). Power failure could possibly work, though Im not sure what the &quot;circumstance&quot; would be. Removing a mechanical arm is a very similar example, but what would this be? Power fails whenever she takes a called shot at her tendrils? Either way, it wouldnt fit above 3 dots, though maybe recieving a called shot is considered &quot;Common&quot;? <br /> <br /> As for Boneless and Brachiation, she's got those, too. Brachiation isnt AS useful (just Wall Crawling), but Boneless is her main core power. Its at lvl 3, +1 for defensive. Im pretty sure im gonna package it into a Monstrous Transformation that is on all the time (Relentless Variation) that she has to suppress with Mimicry (entangled with Concentration).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-14T21:27:54-08:00","id":1497160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1497028-deviant-stretchy-variations?p=1497080#post1497080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh dang, I had forgotten that Directed Variations can't penetrate cover. Woof, that makes some psychic type powers far less useful (telepathy to a degree, telekinesis especially).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would personally say that being able to manipulate the world from thirty feet away is plenty useful without needing to be able to do so through closed windows as well, and Telepathy includes multiple workarounds that allow it to function as it's supposed to even with walls in the way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Power failure could possibly work, though Im not sure what the &quot;circumstance&quot; would be. Removing a mechanical arm is a very similar example, but what would this be? Power fails whenever she takes a called shot at her tendrils? Either way, it wouldnt fit above 3 dots, though maybe recieving a called shot is considered &quot;Common&quot;? </div> </div> </div>A called shot to a limb is sufficiently unchallenging for an assailant to make and requires no special equipment or circumstances to produce. Common is about right for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Im pretty sure im gonna package it into a Monstrous Transformation that is on all the time (Relentless Variation) that she has to suppress with Mimicry (entangled with Concentration). </div> </div> </div>For not the first time, I will point out that the function of Monstrous Transformation is to allow a character to activate a bunch of Variations at the same time at the price of making the whole package Overt; unless you're trying to get around Clade restrictions, the effect is otherwise identical to simply entangling a bunch of Variations with a single Scar and using the Disfiguring Scar Deviation on a different Scar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}